it must be an advantage he could be right strong lungs good respiratory system sure he'll pull

00:38:08.290 --> 00:38:29.400
through come on sit here sir

00:38:30.410 --> 00:38:33.400
Right. Now, listen carefully.

00:38:34.400 --> 00:38:40.060
As I see it, the main problem will be panic when the helmet is removed.

00:38:41.440 --> 00:38:43.680
Colonel Foster's been breathing liquid for some hours now.

00:38:44.810 --> 00:38:48.290
Drugs will have been used to help his lungs adapt.

00:38:49.550 --> 00:38:57.000
Now, when we attempt to reverse to normal, the physical experience will be similar to drowning.

00:38:58.300 --> 00:38:59.960
Unless this moment is carefully...

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:05.450
controlled the patient could go into convulsion and possibly choke let the

00:39:05.450 --> 00:39:27.100
colonel know the situation right if you can hear me nod your head we're going to

00:39:27.100 --> 00:39:29.810
remove your helmet try and maintain

00:39:30.000 --> 00:39:35.250
your rhythm of breathing. Whatever happens, don't panic. Do you understand?

00:40:11.160 --> 00:40:11.600
What is that?

00:40:12.060 --> 00:40:13.760
Two cc's of petrocombe.

00:40:13.940 --> 00:40:14.620
It should help.

00:40:14.940 --> 00:40:15.380
I hope.

00:40:20.340 --> 00:40:21.500
It's the resuscitate already.

00:40:22.070 --> 00:40:22.510
Yes, sir.

00:40:23.060 --> 00:40:23.740
All right, Lieutenant.

00:40:24.380 --> 00:40:24.640
Again.

00:41:37.930 --> 00:41:38.670
Take hold of him.

00:42:09.370 --> 00:42:09.650
